# Append-only files: both sides' new lines are kept, never a conflict.
#
# WHY (2026-08-08): the harness writes bookkeeping on every turn. Without this,
# any worktree lane older than a few hours is GUARANTEED to conflict with main
# on telemetry alone — the lane then parks, and real work strands behind a
# conflict nobody disagreed about. 274 files of work sat stranded across 3 lanes
# because of 14 collisions, most of them two agents appending to the same log.
#
# Rule of thumb: `merge=union` belongs ONLY on files that are strictly
# append-only line records. Never on prose (it duplicates paragraphs) and never
# on structured single-object files (it produces invalid syntax).

# --- Line-delimited JSON: every line is an independent record -----------------
*.jsonl merge=union

# --- Logs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log merge=union
knowledge/log.md merge=union

# --- Deliberately NOT union (prose / structured docs — real resolution needed) -
# PROJECTS.md, guides/INDEX.md, directives/*.md, **/source-ledger.md, *.html
# These carry meaning in their ordering and prose. A collision there is a real
# disagreement and should surface to a human or an agent, not be auto-stitched.
